{"term":"frown","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:05433798ad092a4fb7","definition":"A wrinkling of the forehead with the eyebrows brought together, typically indicating displeasure, severity, or concentration.","example":"Philip had once told him of a man who had a horse-shoe frown, and Tom had tried with all his frowning-might to make a horse-shoe on his forehead","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frownful","frownless","frownsome","frowny","permafrown","turn the frown upside down"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frown#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9be0056c14feb01ce9","definition":"A downturn of the corners of the mouth, typically expressing sadness.","example":"The smile and the frown are both indicated and the operation of a motor driven flasher causes the face to look happy and sad in turn.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Canada, US","register":"Canada, US","wordFamily":["frownful","frownless","frownsome","frowny","permafrown","turn the frown upside down"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frown#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5701df416facce55cf","definition":"Any facial expression that indicates disapproval or displeasure.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["frownful","frownless","frownsome","frowny","permafrown","turn the frown upside down"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frown#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d03604d3a1e9e68da9","definition":"To have a frown on one's face.","example":"She frowned when I told her the news.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["scowl"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["frownful","frownless","frownsome","frowny","permafrown","turn the frown upside down","afrown","frown at","frowner","frown on","frown upon","outfrown"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frown#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:62176cd202d3e1751a","definition":"To manifest displeasure or disapprobation; to look with disfavour or threateningly.","example":"Noisy gossip in the library is frowned upon.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["scowl"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["frownful","frownless","frownsome","frowny","permafrown","turn the frown upside down","afrown","frown at","frowner","frown on","frown upon","outfrown"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frown#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9da76d173a932ae9d0","definition":"To repress or repel by expressing displeasure or disapproval; to rebuke with a look.","example":"Let us frown the impudent fellow into silence.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["scowl"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["frownful","frownless","frownsome","frowny","permafrown","turn the frown upside down","afrown","frown at","frowner","frown on","frown upon","outfrown"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frown#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0fa020d1fa68f9dcc6","definition":"To communicate by frowning.","example":"Frank frowned his displeasure with my proposal.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["scowl"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["frownful",